      "id": "b010",
      "chapter": "s2",
      "kind": "narration",
      "display": {
        "en": "When sunlight hits the tiny molecules of gas in the air, short blue waves bounce around far more than long red waves. This is called Rayleigh scattering. Blue light ends up coming at us from every part of the sky."
      },
